Annotations: |
  This is a self-contained Gradle feature module. Verified decoupled: none of its top-level
  files reference AppDependencies, SignalDatabase, or jobmanager — the module instead
  declares its own narrow NetworkController/StorageController interfaces (implemented by the
  host app) and its own RegistrationDependencies object mirroring the app-wide
  service-locator convention at module scope. State that must survive process death (e.g. a
  killed-and-restored registration flow) is captured entirely in `RegistrationFlowState`.

---

"RegistrationDependencies(networkController: NetworkController, storageController: StorageController, isLinkAndSyncAvailable: Boolean, isPhoneNumberlessRegistrationAvailable: Boolean)":
  location: RegistrationDependencies.kt
  annotations: |
    Module-local dependency injection point, mirroring the app-wide AppDependencies pattern
    at feature-module scope: the module calls out to the host app only through the interfaces
    and callbacks provided here, never through app-module types directly.

    `networkController`: the module's abstraction over whatever network client the host app
    wires up for registration server calls.
    `storageController`: the module's abstraction over persisting in-progress registration state.
    `isLinkAndSyncAvailable`, `isPhoneNumberlessRegistrationAvailable`: feature flags the host
    app resolves and passes in, gating flows that are still being rolled out.
  methods:
    "provide(registrationDependencies: RegistrationDependencies)": |
      Installs the singleton instance the rest of the module reads through get. Must be called
      once, before any other module code runs, typically from the host app's startup path.
    "get() -> dependencies:RegistrationDependencies": |
      The currently-installed instance.

"RegistrationRepository(networkController: NetworkController, storageController: StorageController)":
  location: RegistrationRepository.kt
  annotations: |
    The module's data-access and orchestration layer for the registration/re-registration/
    linked-device/backup-restore flows: every server call and every piece of persisted
    flow state passes through here rather than being called directly from UI/ViewModel code.

    `networkController`, `storageController`: injected via RegistrationDependencies.
  methods:
    "createSession(e164: String) -> result:RequestResult<SessionMetadata, CreateSessionError>": |
      Starts a new registration session for the given phone number.
    "requestVerificationCode(transport: String, e164: String, sessionId: String) -> result:RequestResult<SessionMetadata, RequestVerificationCodeError>": |
      Requests that a verification code be sent to `e164` over `transport` (SMS or voice call)
      for the given session.

      `transport`: delivery channel for the code.
    "submitVerificationCode(code: String, sessionId: String) -> result:RequestResult<SessionMetadata, SubmitVerificationCodeError>": |
      Submits a user-entered verification code against the given session.
    "registerAccountWithSession(sessionId: String, e164: String) -> result:RegisterAccountResult": |
      Completes registration using a verified session (SMS/call verification path).
    "registerAccountWithRecoveryPassword(e164: String, recoveryPassword: String) -> result:RegisterAccountResult": |
      Completes registration using a previously-derived recovery password instead of a fresh
      verification session (the "I still have my AEP" path).
    "restoreMasterKeyFromSvr(e164: String, pin: String, svrCredentials: List<SvrCredentials>) -> result:RestoreMasterKeyResult": |
      Recovers the account's master key from secure value recovery using the user's PIN.
    "saveFlowState(state: RegistrationFlowState)": |
      Persists the entire in-progress flow state, so it can survive process death and be resumed.
    "restoreFlowState() -> state:RegistrationFlowState": |
      Reads back a previously-persisted flow state, if any is still valid.
    "clearFlowState()": |
      Discards any persisted flow state, e.g. after the flow completes or is abandoned.
    "isRegistered() -> registered:Boolean": |
      Whether this device already has a completed local registration.
    "startProvisioning() -> events:Flow<ProvisioningEvent>": |
      Begins the "scan a QR code from a registered device" linked-device provisioning flow and
      streams its progress events.
    "restoreRemoteBackup(aep: AccountEntropyPool) -> progress:Flow<RemoteBackupRestoreProgress>": |
      Downloads and restores a remote (server-hosted) backup using the given account entropy
      pool, streaming progress.

"RegistrationViewModel(repository: RegistrationRepository)":
  location: RegistrationViewModel.kt
  annotations: |
    Holds and evolves `RegistrationFlowState` in response to RegistrationFlowEvents raised by
    the flow's screens, delegating every actual network/storage operation to
    `RegistrationRepository`.

    `repository`: the module's data-access layer, injected.
  methods:
    "applyEvent(state: RegistrationFlowState, event: RegistrationFlowEvent) -> next:RegistrationFlowState": |
      Pure state-transition function: given the current flow state and a raised event, returns
      the next flow state (which screen to navigate to, what data to carry forward).

      `state`: current flow state.
      `event`: the event raised by the current screen (e.g. "code submitted", "restore chosen").
    "getRequiredLinkedDevicePermission() -> permission:String": |
      The runtime permission the linked-device provisioning flow must have granted before it can
      proceed on the current OS version, or none if no additional permission is required.

"RegistrationFlowState(backStack: List<RegistrationRoute>, sessionMetadata: SessionMetadata, storageCapable: Boolean, doNotAttemptRecoveryPassword: Boolean, isRestoringNavigationState: Boolean)":
  location: RegistrationFlowState.kt
  annotations: |
    The complete, persistable state of an in-progress registration/restore flow: navigation
    back-stack, the active session's metadata, verification progress, recovered/generated key
    material, and pending restore-method selection. Fully parcelable so it round-trips through
    RegistrationRepository.saveFlowState/restoreFlowState with no separate serialization step.

    `backStack`: controls which screen is shown and what "back" does.
    `sessionMetadata`: the active registration session, once one exists.
    `storageCapable`: whether the server reported this account already has SVR/PIN data.
    `doNotAttemptRecoveryPassword`: if set, skip the recovery-password path and always create a
    fresh session instead.
    `isRestoringNavigationState`: true while the ViewModel is still deciding whether to resume a
    previously-persisted flow or start fresh.

